{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "section_title", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {}, "render": {"prefix": "\\section{", "suffix": "}\n\\label{section-cofibered-groupoids}"}, "risk_level": "R1", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:1ab7933b5038d6c92cb01a129c8d99780f7f23f5b89cfe7f4f878198fd2f1352", "source_text": "Prorepresentable functors and predeformation categories", "source_text_hash": "sha256:e0f31550b6a5af7070959ef3b68929b8c2171e19efa04093fe3302eb6001bdfa", "unit_id": "tag:06GI:title"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0002": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0004": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0005": "$\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0006": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0007": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{remarks-cofibered-groupoids}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{item-definition-restricting-base-category}", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:4848d57e39c17125cdafbd9837f6c64341a404adb767c032883376b506068dee", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:44026a0d68fad31e53d66377c79aea31215defe40a3d1bbe0c48ba4cfea821f7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nOur basic goal is to understand categories cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0001> and <MATH_0002>. Since\n<MATH_0003> is a full subcategory of\n<MATH_0004> we can restrict categories cofibred in\ngroupoids over <MATH_0005> to <MATH_0006>, see\nRemarks <REF_0001>\n(<REF_0002>).\nIn particular we can do this with functors, in particular with\nrepresentable functors. The functors on <MATH_0007>\none obtains in this way are called\nprorepresentable functors.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:5524e368794e488450e2e48f26b66ae3d2eadac8391414593e646b496f8b7b83", "unit_id": "tag:06GI:prose-0001"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$F$", "MATH_0003": "$F \\cong \\underline{R}|_{\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda}$", "MATH_0004": "$R \\in \\Ob(\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda)$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-prorepresentable}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:82e100444909388180b9ee91637deeadf28e486a45ca3e5c43f6260216508447", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d2c5606a22ed1dfd6a34c7bbefa2645d425ffacf688effcc7071c093f9ead30a", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a functor.\nWe say <MATH_0002> is <TEXTITOPEN_0001>prorepresentable<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> if there exists an isomorphism\n<MATH_0003> of functors for some\n<MATH_0004>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:52f97b2c8355613fd3dec45748d5f230e8fafef4fe229721c34efe9f4c158858", "unit_id": "tag:06GX:statement"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$F : \\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda \\to \\textit{Sets}$", "MATH_0002": "$R \\in \\Ob(\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda)$", "MATH_0003": "$$\nF(k) = \\Mor_{\\widehat{\\mathcal{C}}_\\Lambda}(R, k) = \\{*\\}\n$$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:c826c358edd42ba01d784397ac5313c7c23d7f751b71adc9cba284e79cf626ed", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:4fc869d065ea569a5626a0de72d6d63762067291a4798d9a1bd6b3d24622c8f7", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nNote that if <MATH_0001> is prorepresentable\nby <MATH_0002>, then\n<MATH_0003>\nis a singleton. The categories cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0004> that are arise in deformation theory will often satisfy\nan analogous condition.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c8a048fcb3a4867a3b38e6c109fa9185f90ce614c928d7e04066c14814364e80", "unit_id": "tag:06GI:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "formal-defos", "node_kind": "definition", "parent_tag": "06GI", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$\\mathcal{F}$", "MATH_0002": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "MATH_0003": "$\\mathcal{F}(k)$", "MATH_0004": "$\\mathcal{F}(k)$", "MATH_0005": "$\\mathcal{C}_\\Lambda$", "TEXTITCLOSE_0001": "}", "TEXTITCLOSE_0002": "}", "TEXTITOPEN_0001": "{\\it ", "TEXTITOPEN_0002": "{\\it "}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{definition}\n\\label{definition-predeformation-category}\n", "suffix": "\\end{definition}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:bb8350211fe373cca0f5b84d01f0317d5a592394e76a30c5a3417dd08706f3a3", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:8d6fdbba5c43f018ff6c17d03d6c67a5a6977449d18fc735ad8afe5733f53af0", "source_text": "A <TEXTITOPEN_0001>predeformation category<TEXTITCLOSE_0001> <MATH_0001> is a category cofibered\nin groupoids over <MATH_0002> such that <MATH_0003> is\nequivalent to a category with a single object and a single morphism,\ni.e., <MATH_0004> contains at least one object and there is a\nunique morphism between any two objects. A <TEXTITOPEN_0002>morphism of predeformation\ncategories<TEXTITCLOSE_0002> is a morphism of categories cofibered in groupoids over\n<MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:47e9ab53cdb676fc84a32a912938d18d02d2dae229b3fbf74bc88914b8676ad6", "unit_id": "tag:06GS:statement"}
